M4.21 rebase force-with-lease diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28

Error image
-----------
The first `force-with-lease` push after rebasing M4.21 onto merged M4.20 was
rejected with `stale info`. The remote branch remained at
`958a85be41c602c4c6412a74c66231fce2b6fa1f` while the validated local rebased
commit was `7568a3e`.

Cause
-----
Only `control-main` had been fetched immediately before the rebase. The local
repository therefore lacked a current remote-tracking lease for the M4.21
branch. The command sequence did not use fail-fast shell mode, so the PR base
and draft state were updated after the rejected push. PR #20 was immediately
returned to Draft; no merge occurred.

Risk
----
Git correctly prevented an unproven history rewrite. GitHub still references
the old reviewed M4.21 head and the server remains unchanged. The only risk is
merging the old head if the discrepancy were ignored.

Rollback
--------
No server rollback is required. PR #20 is Draft and unmerged. The remote branch
still has its original commit and can be retained if the rebased update is
abandoned.

Approved correction
-------------------
Verify the remote branch OID is still exactly
`958a85be41c602c4c6412a74c66231fce2b6fa1f`, include this diagnosis in the
rebased commit, and push with an explicit lease bound to that OID. Then require
PR #20 to report the new head, rerun CI, recheck review threads and only then
mark it ready and merge.
